      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the spectrum agree that the Russian threat, exemplified by the intercepted drone over Lithuania, has intensified the urgency of bolstering NATO’s collective defence and accelerating Germany’s move toward the 2 percent spending target and deeper US‑German arms cooperation. At the same time there is a shared recognition that the Bundeswehr’s structural shortcomings – from outdated force concepts to gaps in cyber and hybrid defence – require comprehensive reform, including a reassessment of conscription and a faster procurement cycle for modern platforms such as F‑35s and drones. Finally, all outlets acknowledge that the Ukraine war has reshaped security policy, prompting a consensus that Germany must expand its role in forward deployments and civil‑protective capacities while safeguarding critical infrastructure against emerging aerial and cyber threats.",
